          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: review incomplete—late-event determination is not yet supported\n\nI identified the requested work order and the exact Pending Close timestamp, but the records I am authorized to read contain **no cost-event rows**. This does **not** establish that no late event occurred.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine–Dekoven / Cooler Plate Pack |\n| September cost period | **PER-COST-2025-09** (`Sep-25`) |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Relevant source transaction | Unavailable from authorized records |\n| Event amount | Unavailable |\n| Exact event-created time | Unavailable |\n| Time after Pending Close | Cannot be calculated without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Unavailable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Undetermined** without the event details |\n\nThe Pending Close timestamp is reproduced exactly as recorded; the source does not specify a timezone. The work-order and period details come from the supplied `work_orders` and `cost_periods` records in `system/oracle_scm_cost_management/state.db`.\n\n## Oracle policy\n\nOracle’s **Cost Management 26B**, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” states that newly created transactions relating to the Pending Close period or an earlier period **will not be staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened**. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing after Pending Close.\n\n*Source: supplied Oracle PDF, PDF page 233 / printed page 225.*\n\nAccordingly, withholding processing would be consistent for a newly created, non-exempt September transaction created after **2025-09-30T18:00:00**. I cannot conclude whether the actual recorded status complies because its event type, creation time, and accounting status are unavailable.\n\nThe supporting records require records-custodian access. I requested an authorized extract, but none was provided. The report was saved and submitted as **incomplete / needs evidence**. Completing it requires the work order’s event rows, including source transaction ID, amount, event type, creation timestamp, and accounting status.\n\n**No database records were changed.**",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
